--- !u!114 &1927581092
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1927581090}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Morabaraba is a traditional African strategy board game, particularly
    popular in South Africa and Lesotho. It is a variant of the ancient game of Nine
    Men\u2019s Morris, played by two players on a board consisting of three concentric
    squares connected by lines.\r\n\r\nThe game is played in three distinct phases:\r\n\r\nPhase
    1: Placement.\r\n Each player has 12 pieces (traditionally called \u201Dcows\u201D).
    Players take turns placing one piece at a time on any empty intersection point
    on the board. During placement, players attempt to form \u201Dmills\u201D - three
    pieces in a row along any line on the board.\r\n\r\nPhase 2: Movement\r\n Once
    all pieces have been placed, players take turns moving one piece at a time along
    the lines to an adjacent empty point. Players continue trying to form mills by
    moving their pieces strategically.\r\n\r\nPhase 3: Flying\r\n When a player is
    reduced to 3 pieces, that player may \u201Dfly\u201D their pieces to any empty
    point on the board, not just adjacent ones. This gives the player with fewer
    pieces a fighting chance.\r\n\r\nForming Mills and Capturing.\r\n Whenever a
    player forms a mill (three pieces in a row), they\r\nimmediately capture one
    of their opponent\u2019s pieces by removing it from the board. A piece that is
    part of a mill cannot be captured unless there are no other pieces available.
    The same mill can be \u201Dbroken\u201D and reformed multiple times to capture
    additional pieces.\r\n\r\nWinning the Game: A player wins by reducing their opponent
    to 2 pieces, or by blocking all of their opponent\u2019s possible moves (a position
    where the opponent cannot make a legal move).\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
